  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Envelope 2: Life-Saving Food Assistance to Vulnerable Populations in Northwest Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to contribute to addressing the crucial humanitarian needs of vulnerable conflict-affected populations residing in northwest Syria (NWS) through the provision of food security (FS) assistance. The project will support an estimated 21,000 Internal Displaced Persons (IDPs) (4,200 men, 4,200 women, 6,300 boys, 6,300 girls), including an estimated 3,150 persons with disabilities (PWDs).</narrative>
  </description>
